  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Asialink Promoting Small and Medium-Sized Enterprise Financing through Secured Vehicle Lending Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Asian Development Bank (ADB) will support Asialink Finance Corporation (AFC)&apos;s plan to expand its funding to finance the working capital needs of small and medium-sized enterprises (SMEs) and entrepreneurs, including small and medium-sized enterprises owned by women (WSMEs) and female entrepreneurs in the Philippines. SMEs are critical in driving the country&apos;s economy. However, this customer segment, particularly WSMEs, continues to face significant challenges in terms of access to finance. As part of the project, AFC will implement measures under a gender action plan to support further expansion of access to credit for women.</narrative>
  </description>
